      "heading": "Clinical Evidence: What Does Research Say About SLIN?",
      "body": "<p>Clinical evidence for SLIN focuses on its core ingredients—berberine chromium and gymnema sylvestre. A systematic review of berberine RCTs reported a mean HbA1c reduction of approximately 0.3% and a fasting glucose drop of 10–15 mg/dL (Xie et al. 2022). Chromium supplementation alone has shown modest improvements in insulin sensitivity in type 2 diabetes patients. Gymnema sylvestre has been associated with reduced sweet cravings and improved post‑meal glucose excursions. The evidence base is primarily composed of randomized controlled trials and meta‑analyses providing moderate confidence in the glucose‑lowering potential of these ingredients when combined. However long‑term safety data are limited and most studies have short durations. Action tip: Ask your healthcare provider which lab tests (e.g. HbA1c fasting glucose) and monitoring schedule are right for you.</p>\n",
